      "noCard": true,
      "content": {
        "block1": {
          "blockType": "markdown",
          "content": "<img src='https://raw.githubusercontent.com/RADAR-base/radar-self-enrolment-definitions/refs/heads/dev/projects/STAGING_PROJECT/resources/poster.png' alt='Sleep Hygiene Poster' width='80%'/>"
        },
        "block2": {
          "blockType": "markdown",
          "title": "About The Study of Sleep Hygiene & Health",
          "content": "The Study of Sleep Hygiene & Health (SSHH) is a citizen science research project investigating how smartphone use — particularly before bedtime — influences sleep quality, duration, and overall sleep hygiene.\n<br />By combining wearable device data, smartphone usage information, and short daily questionnaires, we aim to better understand the relationship between digital behaviour and sleep in real-world settings.\n<br />Partners: King's College London, South London and Maudsley NHS Foundation Trust.\n<br />\n<button variant='contained' href='https://raw.githubusercontent.com/RADAR-base/radar-self-enrolment-definitions/refs/heads/dev/projects/STAGING_PROJECT/resources/RADAR_Sleep_Hygiene_PIS.pdf' target='_blank' download='RADAR_Sleep_Hygiene_PIS.pdf'>Learn more</button>"
        }
      }
    },

    {
      "blockType": "column",
      "sx": {
        "width": "100%",
        "paddingTop": "2rem",
        "paddingBottom": "2rem",
        "bgcolor": "background.quaternary",
        "color": "background.quinary",

